Compton is not working you know it's not  working for our kids  the public schools in Compton California  are failing at McKinley Elementary where  Lorena Bautista is Mania Guzman send  their children only half of the students  will graduate high school and only 3%  will attend college the school is very  low and it's not good enough there is no  communication at all whatsoever with the  teachers or with the principal or with a  staff and that is something that needs  to be changed  Ben Austin is a former member of the  California State Board of Education and  the executive director of a nonprofit  group called parent revolution last  summer Compton Unified released the  results of a two-year audit they had  done on themselves and the the the  results were quite shocking we have  evidence that adults are not being held  accountable for their work nor for their  ethical behavior this culture causes us  to have grave concern about the future  of learning opportunities for students  in the district the response from the  Compton School Board President was just  as shocking for me when we see these  results at McKinley where the average  kid is 50 times more likely to drop out  of school than to go to college this is  not a coincidence lacking the resources  to move or pay tuition at private  schools parents in inner-city districts  typically have few options but when  politicians and Sacramento passed a  controversial law last year parents of  children and failing schools finally had  a reason to be hopeful with the goal of  winning federal race to the top dollars  Sacramento politicians passed the parent  trigger law written by former California  senator Gloria Romero the bill passed by  a single vote in both the Senate and the  State Assembly this is about asserting a  right for parents in California our  right very simply known as the parent  trigger which enables parents the right  to petition their own government their  own school  if 51% of parents signed a petition they  can turn their school into a charter  school  replace the staff or use the petition as  a bargaining chip to initiate a  conversation about change we knocked on  to three thousand doors in Compton just  talking to parents and we found quickly  that parents at McKinley elementary were  energized and and wanted to stand up and  stand together and make history where is  suggesting a charter school because the  charter school said the system they work  is really different from a regular  district school parent revolution  introduced the Compton parents to VL  comic Farland the CEO of celerity  educational group VLK told us about the  moment she decided to leave a lucrative  career in the private sector to devote  her life to educating kids in South Los  Angeles at that exact moment in time I  decided to quit my job and go back to  school and get a teaching credential and  applied to Los Angeles Unified School  District to work as a bilingual teacher  with the only caveat that I would need  to be placed in South Los Angeles for  the entire duration of my career like so  many teachers in inner-city public  schools VLK find the experience  frustrating with the goal of making a  bigger difference VLK took a position as  a school administrator only to encounter  bureaucratic resistance at the district  level eventually while working as an  administrator at the district  headquarters in downtown Los Angeles the  ELCA came to the realization that  attempting to change things within the  confines of a traditional public school  system had been a mistake and so a group  of other Los Angeles school district  teachers and other administrators we  decided to open the first celerity  charter school back in South Los Angeles  where we belong and the rest is history  founded in 2005 the celerity charter  schools are already achieving good  results currently students in all for  celerity schools are outperforming the  district schools the otherwise would  have attended no job I really liked the  way they spoke to me the way they  treated us on December 7th 2010 the  Compton parents made history when they  submitted their petition to this  district demanding change the next day  instead of validating the petitions and  standing with the parents for change the  school district Robo called all the  parents called them in for an emergency  meeting and frankly lied to them they  have been dreading us the teacher has  been yelling on us you know telling  other parents don't be doing this unable  to convince enough parents to retract  their signatures from the petition  Compton Unified decided to take a more  direct approach  they sent a registered letter to all  parents requiring that they come in for  an interview so the district could  decide whether the parents were signing  a petition for valid reasons and and  they said in bold underlined letters  that you will be required to show photo  identification such as a driver's  license which is a not even a veiled  threat it's a threat to undocumented  parents that you shouldn't come in and  they didn't instead the parents took the  fight to the courts the day the lawsuit  was filed parent revolution in the  Compton parents held a press conference  in downtown Los Angeles what is due to  my child and every other child in  Compton Unified School District is a  right a right to quality education so  I'm standing for that right we have this  chance now and the faience  I know it's just begun but the thing is  it's begun and it's not going in and so  the judge issued an historic temporary  restraining order preventing the school  district from requiring photo  identification to validate their  petitions the judge agreed with our  argument that it is absurd to make it  more difficult for a parent to sign a  parent trigger petition than it is to  vote for president in the United States  a week after the parents legal victory  the State Board of Education met to  continue discussions about how to  regulate the parent trigger law  dozens of Compton parents traveled in a  school bus overnight to make public  comments at the  the parents knew they were in for a  fight the day after Jerry Brown took  office he replaced seven pro-reform  board members including Ben Austin with  teachers union supporters and Tom  Torlakson the newly elected  Superintendent of Public Instruction was  one of the most outspoken critics of the  parent trigger law in the California  Assembly  I think it's an understatement to say he  was elected with the help of the teacher  the the CTA of the teachers union in  California instead of moving forward  with efforts to write regulations that  began months ago Torlakson put a hold on  the process saying it would be necessary  to pass what he called clean up  legislation I can definitively tell you  one thing that if no one were watching  if this could all go down behind closed  doors they would eliminate the parent  trigger law they would repeal that as  their goal on February 22nd of this year  the compton school board threw another  wrench into the process when they voted  unanimously to reject the parents  petition explaining that they were  unable to verify enough of the parents  signatures for the Compton parents the  outcome is unclear at best what is clear  is that the parent trigger idea is  catching on currently at least 12 other  states are taking a serious look at the  parent trigger option and in California  the parent revolution continues if we're  gonna be real about it we've got to  acknowledge that it is is motherhood and  apple pie as it sounds it's probably the  most radical political agenda in the  state of California as parents that we  cannot probably give them much but the  most parity thing is education  the hook is very important it's the most  important thing that a parent can give  to their child  you
 

